  "id": "cognitive-load",
  "term": "cognitive load",
  "definition": "Cognitive load is the amount and type of mental effort involved in learning or performing a task. In cognitive load theory, it includes load from the material’s inherent complexity, load added by unhelpful instructional demands, and effort that supports building and automating useful mental structures for learning.",
